# Error Presenter & Exception Handling Pattern

- `render_app_error(string $title, string $message, int $code = 500)` — web error view render.
- `AppExceptionHandler` — global CI4 handler, overrides default error page in prod.
- `ErrorPresenter` — formats user-facing error pages.

## Controller (Web request)
```php
try {
    $result = $this->service->do();
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    log_message('error', '[ControllerName::method] ' . $e->getMessage() . ' | user_id=' . session('user_id'));
    return render_app_error('Something went wrong', 'Please try again.', 500);
}
```

## Controller (AJAX/API request)
```php
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    log_message('error', '[ControllerName::ajaxMethod] ' . $e->getMessage());
    return $this->response->setStatusCode(500)->setJSON(['status' => 'error', 'message' => 'Server error.']);
}
```

## Rules
- Services return `['ok' => false]` — they never call `render_app_error()`.
- Never show DB error strings, table names, stack traces in any response.
- Never leave `var_dump`, `dd()`, `print_r` in committed code.
- Log: class, method, error message, user_id, record_id. Never log passwords, tokens, keys.
- Detect AJAX vs Web: `$this->request->isAJAX()` → JSON. Web → `render_app_error()`.
